     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hola Ising,<div><br></div><div>Your very few data of capture-recapture simply &quot;says&quot; that density of your study species is very low... If your data could be analyze with statistical tools, you could find the same conclusion, I think. May be increase of field sampling could confirm this fact... </div><div><br></div><div>saludos</div><div><br></div><div>Salvador Mandujano</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Sep 20, 2017 at 2:06 PM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">secr...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div style=\"border:1px solid #d3d3d3;max-width:850px;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#000000\">\r\n  <div style=\"background-color:#f5f5f5;padding:10px 20px\">\r\n    <table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%\">\r\n      <tbody>\r\n        <tr>\r\n          <td style=\"width:70%\">\r\n            <span style=\"font:18px/20px arial;color:#333333\">\r\n              <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/secrgroup/topics\" style=\"text-decoration:none;color:#333333\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/secrgroup/topics&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487822987000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2NWxKpc61aQyjLXtu0f4oA\">\r\n              secr...@googlegroups.com</a>\r\n            </span>\r\n          </td>\r\n          <td style=\"text-align:right;width:30%\">\r\n            <span style=\"font:20px/24px arial\"><a style=\"color:#dd4b39;text-decoration:none\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email/#!overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail/%23!overview&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487822987000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Ru58sPD0WrnQsWGCwlxv0\">Google Groups</a></span>\r\n          </td>\r\n          <td style=\"width:32px\">\r\n            <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email/#!overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail/%23!overview&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487822987000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Ru58sPD0WrnQsWGCwlxv0\"><img style=\"border:0;vertical-align:middle\" src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/4SGWHe9midrWMDxDIJMQraTMMgnAU71soPZ0D28IOSZcs66TdyRoCqyIhaTt-kwo0YKv2lRo05RkwsGFZdnFhdvy60XdxNlL2U-B=s0-d-e1-ft#http://www.google.com/images/icons/product/groups-32.png\"></a>\r\n          </td>\r\n        </tr>\r\n      </tbody>\r\n    </table>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <div style=\"padding:20px;background-color:#f5f5f5\">\r\n\r\n\r\n<div style=\"font-family:arial;color:#222222;padding:0px\">\r\n  <a name=\"m_-147693137044981869_m_-786731140981366187_digest_top\" style=\"font-size:21px\" rel=\"nofollow\">\r\n  \r\n  \r\n    Topic digest\r\n  \r\n  </a><br>\r\n  <span style=\"font-size:11px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/secrgroup/topics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/secrgroup/topics&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487822987000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2NWxKpc61aQyjLXtu0f4oA\">View all topics</a>\r\n  </span>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font:13px/18px arial;color:#222222;padding:0px;margin-bottom:30px\">\r\n  <ul style=\"margin-left:3px;padding-left:0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <li>\r\n      <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_-147693137044981869_m_-786731140981366187_group_thread_0\" rel=\"nofollow\">\r\n      density estimates from multi sessions (aka study areas)</a> -\r\n      <span style=\"color:#777777\">2 Updates</span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  \r\n  </ul>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <a name=\"m_-147693137044981869_m_-786731140981366187_group_thread_0\" rel=\"nofollow\"></a>\r\n  <div style=\"display:inline-block;font-family:arial;padding:4px 0 5px 0px\">\r\n  \r\n    <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/secrgroup/t/3bb5b1188d102ede?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email\" style=\"font-size:21px;color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/secrgroup/t/3bb5b1188d102ede?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487822987000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2mPFRzxFg-RbJw9h9et0oN\">\r\n      density estimates from multi sessions (aka study areas)\r\n    </a>\r\n  \r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n  <table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;width:100%\">\r\n    \r\n      <tbody><tr><td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\">\r\n          Iding Achmad Haidir &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">idroez...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Sep 20 02:24AM -0700\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        Hi All,<br>\r\n <br>\r\nI am Iding, currently doing camera trapping field work in a Sumatran <br>\r\nrainforest. I have four study areas that each comprises of ~ paired camera <br>\r\ntrap stations. My aims is to estimate density of clouded leopard and <br>\r\nfurther species interaction, temporal and spatial. <br>\r\n <br>\r\nI realized that although with enormous effort that doubled or even <br>\r\nquadrupled, I found little capture and recapture of targeted animal: the <br>\r\nSumatran clouded leopard. I detected individuals 3-5, from each study <br>\r\nareas. Encouragingly, I detected female cloudie in each study area <br>\r\n(session) but not surprisingly, I got very few detection. <br>\r\n <br>\r\nFor the models, I have ran constant model that estimate cloudie density <br>\r\nacross study area as a single population. I therefore would like to focus <br>\r\non how to:<br>\r\n <br>\r\n   1. estimate density of cloudie in each session as independent location <br>\r\n   as each has &gt;60-80 km apart.<br>\r\n   2. include sex as covariate and see if density between male and female <br>\r\n   is different.<br>\r\n   3. estimate sex ratio considered that I have very limited female <br>\r\n   detection.<br>\r\n <br>\r\nFor the analyses, I have been assisted by Mike Meredith but the more I <br>\r\nread, the more I am confused. <br>\r\n <br>\r\nI really appreciate if you could spare your time and thoughts on this <br>\r\nmatter. <br>\r\n <br>\r\nCheers,<br>\r\nIding<br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n      <tr><td style=\"background-color:#ffffff;color:#2e2e2e;font-family:arial;padding:10px 15px;border:1px solid #d3d3d3\">\r\n        <span style=\"color:#b1b0b0;font-size:15px\">\r\n          Murray Efford &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">murray...@gmail.com</a>&gt;: Sep 20 03:06AM -0700\r\n        </span>\r\n        <br><br>\r\n        Dear Iding<br>\r\nThanks for your enquiry. I hate to say this, but I do not think you can <br>\r\nconduct a meaningful capture-recapture analysis of such a sparse dataset. I <br>\r\nknow there are many instances of capture-recapture methods being applied to <br>\r\nvery sparse datasets, but I think we have to be clear that this is <br>\r\nundesirable. Your hard-won data may have to stand on their own without <br>\r\nstatistics, or at most provide a single pooled estimate of density.<br>\r\nRegards<br>\r\nMurray<br>\r\n\r\n      </td></tr>\r\n    \r\n  </tbody></table>\r\n  <div style=\"font-size:11px;margin-bottom:40px;margin-top:5px\">\r\n    <a style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" href=\"#m_-147693137044981869_m_-786731140981366187_digest_top\" rel=\"nofollow\">Back to top</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n  <div style=\"background-color:#f5f5f5;padding:5px 20px\">\r\n  <table cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%\">\r\n  <tbody><tr>\r\n    <td style=\"padding-top:4px;font-family:arial,sans-serif;color:#636363;font-size:11px\">\r\n      \r\n      You have received this digest because you&#39;re subscribed to updates for this group. You can change your settings on the <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source=digest&amp;utm_medium=email#!forum/secrgroup/join\" style=\"color:#1155cc;text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/?utm_source%3Ddigest%26utm_medium%3Demail%23!forum/secrgroup/join&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487822987000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2WSsZd5LpEJ5R4tkEiGzsl\">group membership page</a>.<br>\r\n      To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">secrgroup+unsubscribe@googlegroups.com</a>.\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr></tbody>\r\n  </table>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n"
